      "prompt": "You translate ordinary questions into exactly one read-only DuckDB SELECT or WITH query.\n\nReturn SQL only. Never write files, install software, calculate values yourself, or invent columns.\n\nUse only the supplied schema. Preserve relevant scope from earlier turns unless the newest question changes it.\n\nA requested rate must use its stated numerator and denominator. Percentage-point change means later percentage minus earlier percentage, not relative growth.\n\nWhen the user explicitly asks for percent or percentage, multiply numerator divided by denominator by 100.\n\nWhen the user asks to compare years or groups without asking for a change, keep those year/group columns and requested measures in the output.\n\nWhen several known category values are named, filter them separately with IN rather than concatenating them.\n\nUse NULLIF for denominators. Missing values remain missing and are not zero.\n\nSCHEMA:\nCREATE TABLE \"attendance_2023\" (\n  \"Centre\" VARCHAR,\n  \"Month\" VARCHAR,\n  \"Enrolled Kids\" BIGINT,\n  \"Avg Daily Present\" BIGINT\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE \"attendance_2024\" (\n  \"centre_name\" VARCHAR,\n  \"month\" VARCHAR,\n  \"enrolment\" BIGINT,\n  \"average_attendance\" BIGINT\n);\n\nKNOWN CATEGORICAL VALUES (local or trusted 27B tier only):\n{\"attendance_2023\": {\"Centre\": [\"Chembur Balwadi\", \"Dharavi Balwadi\", \"Govandi Balwadi\", \"Kurla Balwadi\", \"Mankhurd Balwadi\", \"Sion Balwadi\", \"Wadala Balwadi\", \"Worli Balwadi\"], \"Month\": [\"April\", \"August\", \"December\", \"February\", \"January\", \"July\", \"June\", \"March\", \"May\", \"November\", \"October\", \"September\"]}, \"attendance_2024\": {\"centre_name\": [\"Chembur Balwadi\", \"Dharavi Balwadi\", \"Govandi Balwadi\", \"Kurla Balwadi\", \"Mankhurd Balwadi\", \"Sion Balwadi\", \"Wadala Balwadi\", \"Worli Balwadi\"], \"month\": [\"April\", \"August\", \"December\", \"February\", \"January\", \"July\", \"June\", \"March\", \"May\", \"November\", \"October\", \"September\"]}}\n\nCURRENT QUESTION:\ncentre wise attendance percentage for 2023 and 2024 side by side",
      "response": "WITH attendance_2023 AS (\n  SELECT \"Centre\", \"Month\", \"Enrolled Kids\" AS enrolled_2023, \"Avg Daily Present\" AS present_2023\n  FROM \"attendance_2023\"\n),\nattendance_2024 AS (\n  SELECT \"centre_name\" AS Centre, \"month\" AS Month, \"enrolment\" AS enrolled_2024, \"average_attendance\" AS present_2024\n  FROM \"attendance_2024\"\n),\ncombined AS (\n  SELECT \n    a.Centre, \n    a.Month, \n    a.enrolled_2023, \n    a.present_2023, \n    b.enrolled_2024, \n    b.present_2024\n  FROM attendance_2023 a\n  JOIN attendance_2024 b\n  ON a.Centre = b.Centre AND a.Month = b.Month\n)\nSELECT \n  Centre, \n  Month, \n  enrolled_2023, \n  present_2023, \n  enrolled_2024, \n  present_2024,\n  (present_2023 * 100.0 / NULLIF(enrolled_2023, 0)) AS attendance_percent_2023,\n  (present_2024 * 100.0 / NULLIF(enrolled_2024, 0)) AS attendance_percent_2024\nFROM combined\nORDER BY Centre, Month;",
